# Spirit domain (life/spirit_domain.js, builds spirit_gate + spirit_dwelling, dimension ttl:spirit_domain).
# Needs the placer to have run (~1 min after start): `ttl spiritdomain where` must list both builds as placed. Each
# `expect` throws "ttl: expected ..." on a wrong answer, which `server.sh test-all` counts as a failure.
# 1. A Life 1 bot is refused: it is put in the gate's doorway and the log says "[ttl] spirit domain: refused
#    TtlBotSpiritL1 (life1)" (confine.js may bounce it to the Mortal Realm afterwards; either way it is not inside).
# The sleeps after a walk outlast the gate's 4 second cooldown, so the next doorway answers.
# 2. A Life 2 bot enters by `tp`, and by walking into the doorway, and returns through the arch.
ttl spiritdomain where
ttlbot spawn TtlBotSpiritL1
@sleep 2
ttl spiritdomain walk TtlBotSpiritL1 gate
@sleep 2
ttl spiritdomain expect TtlBotSpiritL1 out
ttlbot spawn TtlBotSpirit
@sleep 2
execute as TtlBotSpirit run ttl wish knowledge
execute as TtlBotSpirit run ttl choose slime
@sleep 3
ttl karma TtlBotSpirit expect phase life2
ttl spiritdomain expect TtlBotSpirit out
ttl spiritdomain tp TtlBotSpirit
@sleep 2
ttl spiritdomain expect TtlBotSpirit in
# back through the return arch (the real trigger), then in again by the gate's doorway
ttl spiritdomain walk TtlBotSpirit back
@sleep 5
ttl spiritdomain expect TtlBotSpirit out
ttl spiritdomain walk TtlBotSpirit gate
@sleep 5
ttl spiritdomain expect TtlBotSpirit in
ttl spiritdomain walk TtlBotSpirit back
@sleep 5
ttl spiritdomain expect TtlBotSpirit out
